From ac64721eb614b8f6083616d6af0fdaad2e79b985 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Micheal Waltz <micheal@ecliptik.com>
Date: Mon, 21 Sep 2026 11:17:30 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] DOS-PORT: patch 0186 -- report the campaign counters in the
 run manifest

Consolidates the reporting side of 0125, 0126, 0127, 0133, 0135, 0146, 0150,
0152, 0154, 0155, 0156, 0157, 0158, 0159, 0162, 0167, 0168, 0175, 0176, 0177,
0179, 0180, 0181, 0184, 0185 and 0186. Engine/main/quit.cpp only.

Every counter added by the earlier patches in this series needs a line at
shutdown to be readable at all, and a bracket that is added but never emitted
is exactly the failure this campaign hit once already (RBB1: a cell spent,
nothing printed). So the emit code sits in one place, after everything it
reads.

0146 adds the second defence to the tick-phase writer: a phase that was
entered cannot have taken no time, and one that was never entered is an
instrument that did not fire. Both are flagged in the output rather than
asserted, because a legitimately tiny phase can round to zero microseconds
and a crash there would be worse than a wrong number.

Link dependency: this file declares extern "C" counters defined in
vendor/SDL (dos_port_vblank_*, dos_port_flush_*, dos_port_fb_created), so it
builds only with SDL patch 0177 applied as well. Both series are applied
together by apply-patches.sh.

Provenance of this export (2026-09-21): these edits sat uncommitted in the
vendor tree from patch 0123 onward, which is why every gate cell since said
build_dirty=1. They were made under one campaign-wide patch counter shared
with vendor/SDL, and each hunk carries its number in an in-source comment.
Intermediate states were never committed, so this patch is a hunk-level
partition of the final tree by concern, attributed by those comments -- not a
replay of the order the edits were made in, and its intermediate state was not
built on its own. The numbers named below are the ones found in its hunks.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
